{
  "description": "MAINTAINER RULING #984 at the EIGHTH main-line container found in this slice, and the second that executes no statements. An `each` iteration narrows the addressed set to one turtle and runs a body, so it is a unit of main-line progress exactly as a loop iteration is -- but the boundary that serves every other container fires per STATEMENT, so an empty `each` body had none, and a queued `every` occurrence was stranded. The iteration is now charged against the execution budget and carries the same empty-body boundary; the charge comes BEFORE the narrowing, so an iteration the budget refuses publishes no addressing event. `new_turtle` is a REPORTER (spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:21), so its value MUST be bound for a turtle to exist: a bare `new_turtle` statement creates nothing at all. Two bindings plus the implicit default turtle give three addressed turtles, hence three iterations -- `each` over a single turtle cannot distinguish a per-iteration boundary from a per-statement one. The empty body is the whole point of the fixture and must not be improved into a non-empty one.",
